 \section{Predictions and falsification tests}
 For a held-out binary task satisfying the assumptions, the observed act rate should approach $M(p)$ and conditional correctness should approach $C(p)$ within preregistered sampling uncertainty. The interpretation fails if class balance or calibration is wrong, errors are conditionally dependent, agents use asymmetric thresholds, the latent label is unstable, or abstention changes the data-generating process. Such failures invalidate the operational confidence claim without contradicting the algebra.
